# Shell scripts must always be checked out with LF line endings.
# Bash refuses CRLF on `set -uo pipefail`, here-docs, and continuation
# backslashes, which broke smoke runs on Windows checkouts during
# v0.9.3 closeout. Apply globally so any future script under
# docs/scripts/ or VSAT/**/docs/scripts/ inherits the rule.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Enforce UTF-8 encoding and LF line endings on all Markdown files.
# Added 2026-05-10 to prevent mojibake recurrence (U+FFFD incident from C1.2d-1b initial commit).
# `working-tree-encoding=UTF-8` requires Git 2.10+; checkout will fail-fast if a *.md is encoded otherwise,
# which is the desired behavior for catching mis-encoded edits early.
*.md text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
